gamemaster (0.3.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * A Valheim world is set up in the same steps as a Zomboid world:
    'valheim world create NAME' writes the rules of the world, to be
    edited, 'valheim world init NAME' writes the service, and 'valheim
    start' starts the server, which makes the world. 'world create' no
    longer starts the server.
  * The rules of a Valheim world - preset, combat, death penalty,
    resources, raids, portals, no build cost, player events, passive
    mobs, no map - stand in ~/.config/unity3d/IronGate/Valheim/
    gamemaster/<world>.conf, from the new template template_world.conf,
    and are handed to the server on every start.
  * 'valheim world init NAME' takes over a world the server has already,
    such as one played before GameMaster: it writes the service for it
    and passes no rules, so the world keeps its own. It refuses while a
    server runs, and says how to stop one that GameMaster did not start.
  * A command a program does not know shows the commands there are, then
    an ERROR line, and returns 1 - the same in gamemaster, zomboid and
    valheim. It returned 2 before, without an ERROR line.

 -- AlfaAlf <git@alfaalf-media.de>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200

gamemaster (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Valheim: 'gamemaster install valheim' and 'gamemaster add valheim', and
    the new program 'valheim' to run a server: status, start, stop, update,
    worlds, the players that are online, and the lists of admins, banned
    and permitted players. Valheim has no remote console, so the state of
    a server and its players are read from its log.
  * The agent may run /usr/sbin/valheim through sudo as well.
  * The ports of a new server are checked against the servers of every
    game, and Valheim's second port counts as taken too.
  * gamemaster.conf has new settings VH_APP_ID, VH_DEFAULT_BRANCH and
    VH_DEFAULT_USER. A gamemaster.conf that was changed by hand is kept by
    dpkg; add the three lines there before installing a Valheim server.
  * SOUL.md covers both games; new skills valheim-world, valheim-players,
    valheim-troubleshoot and valheim-knowledge.
  * A quote at the end of a setting is kept unless it closes a quote at
    its start: VH_SERVER_NAME=Halle "Nord" lost its last quote before.
  * The logs below /var/log/gamemaster belong to root and the group of
    the server, readable for the group, so the agent can read them.
    systemd created them for root alone with the service's UMask=0007;
    GameMaster now creates them first and sorts them before every start.
    Zomboid logs that were readable for everyone are now 0640.

 -- AlfaAlf <git@alfaalf-media.de>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0200

gamemaster (0.1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 'gamemaster add zomboid' without -d looks for the server in the home
    directory of the user as well, and says what to do when it finds
    several or none.
  * Skills for AI agents in /usr/share/doc/gamemaster/skills: switching
    worlds, new worlds, mods, restoring a backup, troubleshooting, and
    background knowledge. SOUL.md is shorter and points to them.
  * The service stops the server with SIGINT, as Ctrl+C does, so it saves
    the world when systemd stops it or the machine shuts down. Units
    written by 0.1.6 get it with 'zomboid service'.

 -- AlfaAlf <git@alfaalf-media.de>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:15:00 +0200

gamemaster (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New command 'zomboid fix-permissions': gives everything below ~/Zomboid
    back to the server user. Server/, Saves/ and mods/ may be changed by the
    agent, db/ belongs to the server alone, the rest may be read. Links are
    never followed, only reported.
  * The service runs fix-permissions before every start and the server with
    UMask=0007. Units written by an older version do not have this yet;
    'zomboid world switch' to the loaded world writes them again.
  * 'gamemaster add' and 'install' put the data directory in order.
  * The agent user gets umask 0007 through pam_umask (GECOS field).
  * Files and directories are created as root without following links;
    the database of a world is no longer open to the agent.
  * The data directory is taken from the home of the server user;
    PZ_SERVER_DATA_DIR is no longer read.
  * The configuration of a server can add ExecStartPre, ExecStartPost and
    ExecStopPost commands to its service (PZ_EXEC_START_PRE_1 and so on).
    A command run as root is only accepted when it and every directory
    above it can be changed by root alone; /etc/gamemaster/hooks is there
    for such scripts.
  * New command 'zomboid service': writes the service again from the
    configuration without stopping the server.
  * First unit tests.

 -- AlfaAlf <git@alfaalf-media.de>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200

